  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "He Feng Yang invites him alongside Fairy Cang Yu for the planned attack on Hu Immortal blessed land, naming him a rank seven Gu Immortal with an offensive Immortal Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        669
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fairy_cang_yu",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "sys_immortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "At the sect meeting He Feng Yang still treats him as the greatest battle strength meant to hold the fort with that attacking Immortal Gu, then a letter from the ten sects’ Northern Plains investigation asks for him. He Feng Yang loses that strongest general before he can act, and the elders judge they cannot refuse after True Yang Building collapses.",
      "chapters": [
        697
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "pulled-to-northern-plains",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_he_feng_yang",
        "reg_northern_plains",
        "house_eighty_eight_true_yang_building"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Second supreme elder later reads Feng Jiu Ge’s loan of one’s own way Immortal Gu as paired with taking Old Lord Can Yang away to weaken Immortal Crane Sect’s fight for Hu Immortal blessed land.",
      "chapters": [
        698
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "feng-jiu-ges-pairing",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_feng_jiu_ge",
        "gu_ones_own_way_immortal_gu",
        "fac_immortal_crane_sect",
        "loc_hu_immortal_blessed_land"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "With Feng Jiu Ge leading, he stands among Central Continent Gu Immortals before saint regional wall and helps open the passage: he blows a candle-like Immortal Gu so glittering light spots melt a sixty-three step path, then urges the group onward toward Northern Plains’ licorice regional wall.",
      "chapters": [
        710
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "saint-regional-wall",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_central_continent"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Immortal Crane Sect treats his battle strength as top five in the sect, and the collapse of Eighty-Eight True Yang Building is important enough that the sect sends him to Northern Plains to investigate. There he uses the immortal killer move life chasing fire, the method that made his name shake Central Continent. The faint yellow flame traces auras back to attackers, burns body and immortal aperture, and uses life as fuel so it keeps burning until special means extinguish it or life force runs out.",
      "chapters": [
        791
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "killer-move-burns-three-enemies",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan disguises as him, not as Feng Jiu Ge, to spring the trap that captures Hei Cheng.",
      "chapters": [
        990
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "disguise-for-hei-chengs-trap",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "char_hei_cheng"
      ]
    }
  ],
